  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::3749",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with potassium channels through a shared mechanism involving delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. The evidence suggests that Guanidine binds to Kcna6, Kcnv2, and Kcna7, all of which participate in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, which in turn is associated with Kcnc4. This indicates a potential pathway where Guanidine may modulate potassium channel function, leading to changes in Kcnc4 activity. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the specific target of Guanidine remains unclear. The overlapping involvement of these potassium channels in delayed rectifier activity implies that Guanidine may influence Kcnc4 through a common regulatory mechanism, possibly by altering channel function or expression. This integrated evidence supports a role for Guanidine in modulating Kcnc4 activity through potassium channel interactions.",
